{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Their king.</b> The lamed has a dagesh because of the loss of the heh of the demonstrative, and they are two words, like מזה (from what) [ibid. 4:2]." "<b>You grind.</b> Like תשחקו (you play/mock), by way of metaphor for shame and disgrace."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The lemma מלכם in context reflects מה מלכם; Ibn Ezra explains the dagesh in the lamed as compensatory for the dropped heh of מה."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:54.624393876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}